  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "as of rev 7921 (",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-68#icft=FCREPO-68"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": "), the fedora.home context-param is effectively required, although fedora.server.ServerController.init() and fedora.common.Constants.FedoraHome.getValue() suggests otherwise:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Determines the value of \"Fedora Home\" based on the",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "servlet.fedora.home system property (checked first)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "fedora.home system property (checked next) or the",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "FEDORA_HOME environment variable (checked last).",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "However, ServerController.init() uses System.setProperty on the key \"servlet.fedora.home\" to the value of the fedora.home context-param defined in web.xml. If the context-param is not present in web.xml, a NullPointerException is raised (since getServletContext().getInitParameter(\"fedora.home\") would return null). If the context-param is empty, servlet.fedora.home is set to the empty string and the other two options (fedora.home system property and FEDORA_HOME environment variable) are never evaluated. Effectively, the fedora.home context-param is the only way to define \"Fedora Home\".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
